! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: an unfenced AI-and-explanation project can expand into platform and model development and make its schedule unrealistic.
  + context: Minted as a marked self-derived fallback after A5's external-first search found no project statement of this specific problem.
  + IF:
    A six-month pilot evaluates AI-assisted explanation work.
  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, verbatim from the source pattern: “Without explicit scope fences, a project framed around “AI and explanation” can drift into trying to develop storage, user interfaces, or new models, making the schedule unrealistic.” (source: futon3 library/ai4ci/pilot-feasibility.flexiarg:25-27)
  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for pilot-scope mechanisms.
  + BECAUSE:
    The source class makes the circular provenance mechanically visible.
